{
  "requirement": "Listing and reading failures return errors, distinct from successful empty\nlistings and successful reads of empty files.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover both halves of `requirements.sdk.sources.provider.errors`: failures are returned as errors, and they are distinct from successful empty results. I did not request implementation source. The expected behavior comes from the requirement text.\n\n**Listing and reading failures return errors**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[failed_provider_operations_never_become_successful_empty_results]` runs a `FailingProvider` in both modes. In one mode listing fails, and in the other listing succeeds but reading fails.\n  - `search_text` returns an `Err` whose message is \"listing failed\" or \"reading failed\" to match the mode.\n  - `parse` returns \"reading failed\".\n  - `search_structure` returns the matching error message.\n  - So a provider failure is never turned into an empty result in either mode.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` checks real `Sources` failures with `is_err` assertions:\n  - listing a root that is a file;\n  - listing a missing root;\n  - listing a missing scope;\n  - reading a missing file;\n  - reading `../outside.txt`, an absolute path, and a parent-relative path;\n  - an invalid text pattern in a search.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors]` adds more failures:\n  - listing the default scope fails because of a broken `.gitignore`;\n  - reading a file under that broken ignore fails;\n  - listing a scope that contains a symlink fails (unix only).\n  It also checks the success case, where a scoped listing that avoids the broken directory succeeds.\n- `completeness_is_false_only_when_a_match_is_omitted_and_errors_propagate` checks that an invalid regex and invalid UTF-8 or unknown-language parsing return errors.\n\n**Successful empty results are distinct from errors**\n- `successful_empty_listing_and_empty_resources_are_distinct_from_errors` uses a `Primitives` provider with an empty listing and with a one-entry listing of empty text.\n  - `list` returns `Ok` with 0 or 1 entries.\n  - `read` returns `Ok` with empty bytes.\n  - `parse` returns `Ok` with an empty source.\n  - `search_text` and `search_structure` return `Ok` with `complete` true and no matches.\n- `empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct` also checks that an empty directory lists as `Ok` and empty, and that an empty file reads as `Ok` with empty bytes. In the same test, a file root fails to list, which separates the error case from the empty one.\n\nNo obligation, failure case or distinction named in the text lacks a test with an assertion, and all the tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement.",
